 {:runtime "NBB outer orchestration and closed CLJS data boundaries; keep pure shapes/comparisons in .cljc. Native buffer object identity and final editor check/mutation require a minimal reviewed Emacs Lisp shim inside the selected existing server, not an NBB-side imitation."
  :ownership "Oikos owns the consumer adapter and frozen contract use. Spacemacs/private-layer owner owns editor integration; existing i3 owner owns IPC/lifetime integration; GovOne owns governance/auth, with Knoxx as an existing client seam; Muse owns exposure compilation only. Cross-owner implementation changes need their own scoped authorization."
  :client-input "Client supplies only the frozen closed named request and an opaque approval reference through a future separately versioned outer protocol. Do not extend the frozen request schema with raw Lisp, IPC, file paths, socket names, executable paths, scopes, resource facts or dispatcher selectors."
  :outer-protocol
  {:status :proposal-not-implemented
   :version-proposal "oikos.dispatch/v1"
   :request-fields [:protocol-version :request-id :contract-version :contract-digest
                    :named-request :approval-reference]
   :trusted-context "Actor/session, target endpoint and generation, current scope/allowlists, owner admission, native resource facts and verified consent are injected independently by authenticated owners, never accepted from the client's map. Treat transported positive preconditions as advisory."
   :serialization "Explicit bounded UTF-8 JSON data framing at the host boundary, fixed enum mapping to frozen Clojure keywords, strict unknown/duplicate-field rejection and exact integer/range checks. No EDN tagged readers, Lisp reader, executable code or host object in the wire payload. Encoding changes do not change contract semantics. Review exact framing, size ceilings and Unicode handling before implementation."
   :emacs-transport "Prefer an owner-provided named fixed transport. If the existing emacsclient transport is selected, NBB must use shell-free explicit argv to a pinned client/socket, a nonempty reviewed failing alternate-editor, and only a constant audited dispatch wrapper with strictly encoded inert data, never caller-provided forms or function names. An internal fixed wrapper is not a published arbitrary --eval tool. This is a transport design candidate, not permission to call emacsclient or install a handler."
   :bb-transport "If retaining owner BB IPC helpers, cross a fixed versioned subprocess argv/exit-status/data protocol; never pass shell/command strings or import BB/JVM libraries into NBB. The historical S1A BB transport remains HELD, not implicitly qualified by this plan."
   :responses "New closed runtime response schema must distinguish refusal, bounded read, applied mutation and indeterminate-after-transport-loss. Frozen preconditions-satisfied is never renamed to authorized/applied. Bound encoded envelope and decoded content separately; no raw exceptions, private buffers, full trees, credential data or ungoverned output."
   :publication :held}
  :native-editor-identity
  {:buffer "Server-owned registry maps an opaque incarnation to the actual live buffer object using object identity, not name, file path, client UUID or copied buffer-local variables. Creation of a new object, even under the same name, gets a new incarnation; kill invalidates the old registry entry. Deny indirect/shared-text aliases and any unregistered buffer; synthetic fixtures must never alias operator text. No buffer enumeration is required or authorized."
   :epoch "Server/dispatcher owner issues an unpredictable epoch and binds endpoint/generation. Server restart, registry loss/shim reload or reconnect-invalidated session must invalidate old approvals; fail closed until fresh owner registration. Exact server-epoch versus connection-lease semantics must be fixed by the owner without reinterpreting the frozen identity."
   :revision "Measure actual native content modification state inside the buffer; evaluate buffer-chars-modified-tick/buffer-modified-tick and hook behavior in the exact selected Emacs. Define a monotone owner revision and account for edits, undo, revert, narrowing, text properties and indirect aliases. Never trust a client revision counter. Proposed native primitives are not runtime-verified here."
   :range "Widen only the owned target under save-restriction, without selecting it or affecting operator windows. Contract offsets are zero-based half-open bytes of strict UTF-8 text, not Lisp character positions, JS UTF-16 units or necessarily Emacs internal multibyte offsets. Derive exact character-boundary mapping from actual strict UTF-8 encoding, reject mid-codepoint endpoints and invalid/non-scalar/raw-byte representations; no normalization or newline conversion. Do not equate byte-to-position/position-bytes with external UTF-8 without exact-version proof."
   :bounds "Recompute current full buffer UTF-8 length <=1048576, requested span <=4096 and replacement UTF-8 length <=4096; ensure resulting full buffer <=1048576. Reads copy only the allowed exact range without properties; no full-buffer content crosses into NBB or diagnostics."
   :atomicity "Inside one serialized native handler, verify authenticated execution fence, epoch, actual object, native revision, exact request, scope/ownership and current approval, then perform the bounded mutation without yielding. Audit hooks/timers/process filters/reentrancy; a single event loop or NBB mutex alone is not proof. Use native transactional change/rollback only with tested zero-side-effect refusal, and deny read-only/unsupported hook states. Never blindly suppress security hooks or call arbitrary mode commands. Final check must be inside the otherwise-working mutator, not only before IPC."
   :read-atomicity "Read scope, object identity, revision, byte boundaries and bounded content snapshot must be checked/copied within the same native boundary. Before returning, apply current governed output admission; revocation/outage must not leak a previously collected result."}
  :authority-and-consent
  {:needed-from-existing-owners
   [:authenticated-tenant-principal-system-session-to-oikos-actor-binding
    :current-operation-scopes-and-exact-resource-ownership-allowlists
