   :binding "Consent binds exact actor, operation and every argument including literal replacement text and range, contract version/digest, endpoint/generation, server epoch, native buffer/window incarnation and exact revision/cut. Owner identity is not inferred from Linux UID, loopback, model/harness name or caller-provided approval ID."
   :one-use "Use owner-authenticated approval plus a dispatcher-owned operational claim/consumption registry, not a new policy or ledger authority. Define a linearization point for current owner admission/revocation and the native execution fence. A check-then-remote-call race is not solved by comparing a signed map twice. No successful runtime path until owner and dispatcher protocols establish that fence."
   :attempts "Serialized atomic claim permits at most one attempt; replay/concurrent reuse denies. Consume or terminally invalidate before any possible mutation, including crash/reply-loss paths. If outcome cannot be established, report indeterminate, do not retry or reissue an equivalent grant automatically. Restart/epoch loss invalidates outstanding approvals rather than forgetting use and allowing replay."
   :retention "Transient approvals/previews can contain replacement text and linkable identifiers. Keep private and bounded, with owner-set expiry; evidence uses minimum safe references/status, not buffer content or raw approval payloads. No new Clio append, event authority or durable approval store is authorized now."
   :no-substitution "Synthetic approval maps and stubs may test pure contracts/denials only. They cannot qualify authenticated consent, GovOne admission or runtime mutation success. Agent-owned status narrows eligibility but does not bypass frozen explicit mutation-approval binding."}
